1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,580
Learning NEAR is hard.

2
00:00:01,580 --> 00:00:05,281
The docs assume you know crypto, and explainers are static.

3
00:00:05,281 --> 00:00:07,920
Book of NEAR lets you do the real thing.

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:11,256
A first visit starts with three questions.

5
00:00:11,256 --> 00:00:16,920
They pick your path: newcomer, crypto veteran or developer.

6
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:21,775
Demo mode simulates the chain in your browser, so you need no wallet.

7
00:00:21,775 --> 00:00:30,920
Build, sign and send a transaction, and watch it reach Final.

8
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:34,137
Give an app a key that can do only one thing.

9
00:00:34,137 --> 00:00:44,920
Then the app is hacked: the chain refuses each attack and says why.

10
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:48,999
Every lesson has a flat view and a 3D pop-up book.

11
00:00:48,999 --> 00:01:05,920
Follow a recorded testnet transaction hop by hop across shards, chunks and blocks.

12
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:08,794
Deploy a contract in one click, call it,

13
00:01:08,794 --> 00:01:23,920
then watch a cross-contract callback catch a failure.

14
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:28,028
Chain Signatures: one NEAR account signs for Ethereum.

15
00:01:28,028 --> 00:01:33,273
Derive an address, get a signature, and check it recovers to that address.

16
00:01:33,273 --> 00:01:43,920
In demo mode the app plays the signing network; the math is real.

17
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:47,249
Ask for a cross-chain swap with an intent.

18
00:01:47,249 --> 00:01:51,751
In demo mode it is a recorded example quote, not a live price.

19
00:01:51,751 --> 00:01:54,920
No money moves.

20
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:58,375
Every lesson ends with an honest take on NEAR.

21
00:01:58,375 --> 00:02:07,920
Finish a stage to claim its badge: an NFT on testnet, kept in your browser in demo mode.

22
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:13,920
Try it: book-of-near.pages.dev. Demo mode needs no wallet.
